For the first time, Sofia’s composure wavers. She looks away for a moment, then back at you, her voice quieter than before.

<b>The night before she died, Sheila told me something… something I think you need to know.</b> She inhales sharply before speaking the next words. <b>She was pregnant.</b>
She folds her arms, as if bracing herself, but her voice remains steady.

<b>She was scared. Not because she didn’t want the child, but because she wasn’t sure how to handle it. She trusted me to help her figure it out.</b> Her fingers tighten against her sleeves. 
<b>I told her she wasn’t alone. That I would stand by her no matter what. And then… the next day, she was gone.</b> She finally looks at you again, her expression unreadable.
<b>Whoever did this to her, they took more than just one life. Find them.</b>